          desc: '''Each bit of the field `drive_strength` shall read back 0 where the pad's type does not keep that bit.'''
          source: [
            '''[Pad Attributes](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling.hjson](hw/top_darjeeling/data/top_darjeeling.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_attr"
          checks: ["unsupported bits read 0 (assert_PadAttr_UnsupportedBitsRead0)"]
          why: '''The check requires each bit of `drive_strength` to read back a written 0, and 0 on every pad of its type once one read a written 1 as 0.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_ATTR_10
          desc: '''After reset, each pad's attribute output shall be its reset value, 0 in fields its type does not keep. All are 0 but the fields the `attrs` of the pad's top entry set.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_ATTR'''
            '''!!DIO_PAD_ATTR'''
            '''[top_darjeeling.hjson](hw/top_darjeeling/data/top_darjeeling.hjson)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling.hjson](hw/top_darjeeling/data/top_darjeeling.hjson)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling.hjson](hw/top_darjeeling/data/top_darjeeling.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_attr"
          checks: ["reset attributes (assert_PadAttr_ResetAttributes)"]
          why: '''Until the pad's first attribute write after reset, the check compares the pad's attribute output with the reset attributes.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Sleep retention'''
      conditions: [
        '''"pad" is MIO pad `p` or DIO pad `d`; "status bit" is its bit in `MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS` or `DIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS`. "Sleep entry" is a rise of `sleep_en_i`. The mode rows hold while no TAP owns the pad and the sleep mode is unchanged since sleep entry.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_01
          desc: '''At sleep entry, the status bit of every pad whose sleep enable is 1 shall become 1, unless a software clear of that bit lands in the same cycle (`REQ_SLP_09`).'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_EN.EN'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["bit set at entry (assert_PadSleep_BitSetAtEntry)"]
          why: '''For every sleep entry with the sleep enable at 1 and no software clear of the bit, the check requires the status bit to be 1 in the next cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_02
          desc: '''A status bit shall become 1 only at sleep entry, and only if the pad's sleep enable is 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["bit set only at entry (assert_PadSleep_BitSetOnlyAtEntry)"]
          why: '''For every rise of a status bit the check requires a sleep entry with the pad's sleep enable at 1 in the cycle before.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_03a
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 0, a pad's output shall be 0.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["tie low in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieLowInSleep)"]
          why: '''While the status bit is 1 with mode 0 taken at the entry, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 0 in the same cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_03b
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 0, a pad's output enable shall be 1, so the pad drives 0.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["tie low in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieLowInSleep)"]
          why: '''While held in mode 0, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 1.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_04a
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 1, a pad's output shall be 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["tie high in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieHighInSleep)"]
          why: '''While the status bit is 1 with mode 1 taken at the entry, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 1 in the same cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_04b
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 1, a pad's output enable shall be 1, so the pad drives 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["tie high in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieHighInSleep)"]
          why: '''While held in mode 1, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 1.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_05a
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 2, a pad's output enable shall be 0: the pad is high-Z.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["high-Z in sleep (assert_PadSleep_HighZInSleep)"]
          why: '''While the status bit is 1 with mode 2 taken at the entry, the check compares the output enable of a pad no TAP owns with 0 in the same cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_05b
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 2, a pad's output shall be 0.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["high-Z in sleep (assert_PadSleep_HighZInSleep)"]
          why: '''While held in mode 2, the check compares the output of a pad no TAP owns with 0.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_06a
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 3, a pad shall keep the output it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["keep holds (assert_PadSleep_KeepHolds)"]
          why: '''While held in mode 3, the check compares a pad's output with its output at the sleep entry that set the bit, if no TAP owned it then or now.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_06b
          desc: '''While its status bit is 1 and its sleep mode is 3, a pad shall keep the output enable it drove in the last cycle before the bit became 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_MODE.OUT'''
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["keep holds (assert_PadSleep_KeepHolds)"]
          why: '''While held in mode 3, the check compares a pad's output enable with its enable at the sleep entry that set the bit, if no TAP owned it then or now.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_07
          desc: '''Once 1, a status bit shall stay 1 until software writes 0 to it, whatever `sleep_en_i`, the sleep enable and the peripheral do.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN'''
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["bit holds until cleared (assert_PadSleep_BitHoldsUntilCleared)", "clear releases (assert_PadSleep_ClearReleases)"]
          why: '''The first fails a bit at 1 that falls without a software clear; the second requires 0 in the cycle after a clear.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_08
          desc: '''While its status bit is 0, an MIO pad shall drive what its output select names, and a DIO pad the output and output enable of its own peripheral.'''
          source: [
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "sleep_release"
          checks: ["tie 0 drives 0 (assert_PadOutput_Tie0Drives0)", "tie 1 drives 1 (assert_PadOutput_Tie1Drives1)", "select 2 is high-Z (assert_PadOutput_Select2IsHighZ)", "drives selected output (assert_PadOutput_DrivesSelectedOutput)", "no output is high-Z (assert_PadOutput_NoOutputIsHighZ)", "DIO drives its peripheral (assert_PadOutput_DioDrivesItsPeripheral)"]
          why: '''Each holds while the bit is 0.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_09
          desc: '''When sleep entry sets a status bit in the cycle software writes 0 to that bit, the bit shall end 0: software's clear wins.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS'''
            '''[Type RW](util/reggen/README.md#type-rw)'''
            '''[Simultaneous SW and HW access](util/reggen/README.md#simultaneous-sw-and-hw-access)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["clear wins (assert_PadSleep_ClearWins)"]
          why: '''For a sleep entry with the sleep enable at 1 in the cycle of a software clear of the bit, the check requires the bit to be 0 in the next cycle.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_10a
          desc: '''A write to a pad's sleep mode while its status bit is 1 shall leave the pad as it is.'''
          source: [
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["mode write while held (assert_PadSleep_ModeWriteWhileHeld)"]
          why: '''After a sleep mode write while the bit is 1, the check requires the pad to keep the sleep value of the mode taken at the entry.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_SLP_10b
          desc: '''After a write to a pad's sleep mode while its status bit is 1, the new mode shall act at the next sleep entry.'''
          source: [
            '''[Retention Logic](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-logic)'''
            '''[Sleep Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#sleep-features)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "pad_sleep"
          checks: ["tie low in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieLowInSleep)", "tie high in sleep (assert_PadSleep_TieHighInSleep)", "high-Z in sleep (assert_PadSleep_HighZInSleep)", "keep holds (assert_PadSleep_KeepHolds)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''Each uses the mode taken at entry; the CSR checker checks the write is kept.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Register locks'''
      conditions: [
        '''"lock" is one bit of a `*_REGWEN` register; it locks the registers of the same index, and is open at 1 and closed at 0. The rule that a locked pad's attributes do not change (`REQ_LOCK_03a`, `REQ_LOCK_03b`) holds except on a JTAG pad while a TAP owns it.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_01a
          desc: '''Every lock shall read 1 after reset.'''
          source: [
            '''the register description: the `EN` field of each `*_REGWEN`, e.g. !!MIO_PAD_ATTR_REGWEN.EN `resval: "1"`, on `clk_i` with `rst_ni` ([pinmux.hjson `clocking`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/pinmux.hjson))'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''After reset the CSR checker expects every lock, bit 31 of `ALERT_TEST` included, at 1 and compares its value and read with it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_01b
          desc: '''Once software writes 0 to a lock, the lock shall stay 0 until reset.'''
          source: [
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
            '''[Pad Attributes](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker predicts each lock as `rw0c`: an accepted write of 0 clears it and nothing sets it; a lock that returns to 1 before a reset fails the compare.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_01c
          desc: '''A write of 1 to a lock that is 0 shall not reopen it.'''
          source: [
            '''the register description: each lock `rw0c`'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
            '''[Pinmux Configuration](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#pinmux-configuration)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker predicts each lock as `rw0c`, which keeps a closed lock at 0 over a write of 1; a lock that such a write reopens fails the compare.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_02
          desc: '''While a lock is 0, a write to a register it locks shall leave that register unchanged.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PERIPH_INSEL_REGWEN.EN'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["locked read-back holds (assert_Regwen_LockedReadBackHolds)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker holds a register whose lock reads 0 over writes; _locked read-back holds_ decides the attribute registers.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_03a
          desc: '''While a pad's attribute lock is 0, its attribute output shall not change.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_ATTR_REGWEN.EN'''
            '''[Pad Attributes](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "regwen"
          checks: ["locked attribute holds (assert_Regwen_LockedAttributeHolds)"]
          why: '''It holds the pad's attribute output over every cycle its lock is closed, on a pad no TAP owns.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_LOCK_03b
          desc: '''While a pad's attribute lock is 0, what its attribute register reads back shall not change.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PAD_ATTR_REGWEN.EN'''
            '''[Pad Attributes](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/programmers_guide.md#pad-attributes)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "regwen"
          checks: ["locked read-back holds (assert_Regwen_LockedReadBackHolds)"]
          why: '''It holds each pad's read-back over every cycle its lock is closed, an owned JTAG pad included.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Register block and bus'''
      conditions: [
        '''a "failed request" is one whose command integrity code does not match, or a write whose data integrity code does not match ([Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)). No row checks the response or the alert of a read whose only mismatch is in its data code. The "in-band reset" is the alert handler's re-initialization. During it, the handler puts a signal integrity error on its ping and acknowledge pairs on purpose ([Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)). An "illegal combination of address, size and mask" is an address not aligned to its size, a size above 2, or a mask bit set outside the access. It is also a `PutFullData` mask with a lane of the access at 0.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_REG_01a
          desc: '''Every register field shall act as its access type says on software reads and writes answered without an error, a write while its lock reads 1 or it has none.'''
          source: [
            '''the register description: each field's `swaccess`, e.g. !!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS `swaccess: "rw0c"`'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["read-back changes only on a write (assert_PadAttr_ReadBackChangesOnlyOnAWrite)", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker predicts each field from its access type, the pad_attr check the attribute registers.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_REG_01b
          desc: '''Every register field shall read its register description reset value after reset.'''
          source: [
            '''the register description: each field's `resval`, e.g. !!MIO_PAD_SLEEP_STATUS.EN `resval: "0"`'''
            '''[Configuration and Register Definition File Format](util/reggen/README.md#configuration-and-register-definition-file-format)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "fpv_csr_rw"
          checks: ["the CSR checker"]
          why: '''After reset the CSR checker expects each field at its reset value; _reset attributes_ decides the attribute registers.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_01a
          desc: '''The pinmux shall answer every request with one response, and only one.'''
          source: [
            '''TileLink 1.9.3 p. 39: "Receipt of request messages must result in the eventual receipt of a response message by the requestor."; p. 30: "it is illegal to receive a response without receiving the request."; p. 46: "In TL-UL, every message fits within a single beat"'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules (assert_Bus_DeviceRules)"]
          why: '''The TL-UL ABVIP's device rules match each response on the pinmux's port to one open request.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_01b
          desc: '''The pinmux shall answer every request by the TL-UL rules with a response that carries the request's source ID.'''
          source: [
            '''[Source ID requirements for device elements](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#source-id-requirements-for-device-elements)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["device rules (assert_Bus_DeviceRules)"]
          why: '''The TL-UL ABVIP's device rules compare each response's `d_source` with its request's `a_source`.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_01c
          desc: '''Only a failed request, a case of `REQ_BUS_10a` to `REQ_BUS_10d` or one to an address no register maps shall get an error.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on a request not failed exactly for a listed cause.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_02a
          desc: '''Every response shall carry the response integrity code over its op code, size and error.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` BUS.INTEGRITY](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/pinmux.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["response codes correct (assert_Bus_ResponseCodesCorrect)"]
          why: '''It recomputes the response code from each response's opcode, size and error with the shared encoder and compares it with the code sent.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_02b
          desc: '''Every response shall carry the data integrity code over its data.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[pinmux.hjson `countermeasures` BUS.INTEGRITY](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/pinmux.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["response codes correct (assert_Bus_ResponseCodesCorrect)"]
          why: '''It recomputes the data code over each response's data with the shared encoder and compares it with the code sent.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_03
          desc: '''A failed request shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
            '''[cip_base_vseq](hw/dv/sv/cip_lib/README.md#cip_base_vseq)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["failed request errors (assert_Bus_FailedRequestErrors)"]
          why: '''It requires `d_error` 1 on the response to every failed request.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_04
          desc: '''A failed write shall change no register.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of User Bits](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-user-bits)'''
          ]
          kind: "RTL"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["failed write changes nothing (assert_Bus_FailedWriteChangesNothing)"]
          why: '''It holds every register over a failed write, but for an AON field taking an earlier write not yet landed.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_05
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, a failed request shall raise the fatal alert `fatal_fault`.'''
          source: [
            '''[pinmux.hjson `alert_list` fatal_fault](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/pinmux.hjson)'''
            '''[Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["failed request alerts (assert_Alert_FailedRequestAlerts)"]
          why: '''It requires an alert event on `alert_tx_o` within 40 cycles of every failed request.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_06
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, once raised, the fatal alert shall be sent again and again until reset.'''
          source: [
            '''[Alerts per Module](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#alerts-per-module)'''
            '''[Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["fatal alert repeats (assert_Alert_FatalAlertRepeats)"]
          why: '''After a failed request it requires an alert event within 40 cycles of every cycle, until reset.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_07
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, a write of 1 to `ALERT_TEST` bit 0 not answered with an error, while its bit 31 is 1, shall send one alert event.'''
          source: [
            '''The register page says of bit 0: "Write 1 to trigger one alert event of this kind." (!!ALERT_TEST)'''
            '''[Test Alert Register Creation](doc/contributing/hw/comportability/README.md#test-alert-register-creation)'''
            '''[Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["test sends an event (assert_Alert_TestSendsAnEvent)", "no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''Each alert test needs an event within 40 cycles, and each event uses up one test credit, so one test gives one event.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_08
          desc: '''Outside the alert handler's in-band reset, while `ALERT_TEST` bit 31 is 0, a write to its bit 0 that is not a failed request shall send no alert.'''
          source: [
            '''The register page says of bit 31: "Write 0 to disable alert testing until the next reset." (!!ALERT_TEST)'''
            '''[Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''A write of bit 0 while bit 31 of `ALERT_TEST` is 0 sets no test credit, so an alert event with no other cause fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_09
          desc: '''Outside the in-band reset and apart from ping answers, the fatal alert shall be sent only after a failed request or an alert test.'''
          source: [
            '''[pinmux.hjson `alert_list` fatal_fault](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/pinmux.hjson)'''
            '''[Employed Solution](hw/top_earlgrey/ip_autogen/alert_handler/doc/theory_of_operation.md#employed-solution)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "alert"
          checks: ["no alert without a cause (assert_Alert_NoAlertWithoutACause)"]
          why: '''It allows an alert event only after a failed request or against a ping or test credit, one per event.'''
          milestone: "V2S"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_10a
          desc: '''A request with an *undefined opcode* shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Usage of Opcode, Size and Mask](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#usage-of-opcode-size-and-mask)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on an undefined opcode, which the run leaves free.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_10b
          desc: '''A request with an *illegal combination of address, size and mask*, as the Conditions above defines it, shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''TileLink 1.9.3 p. 51: "a_address must be aligned to a_size."'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on an illegal fit, masks kept contiguous in the run.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_10c
          desc: '''A *write of 8 or 16 bits to an address not aligned to a word* shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on an 8 or 16 bit write not aligned to a word.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_10d
          desc: '''A *write narrower than its register*, whose width the location of its fields sets, shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on a write narrower than its register.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_10e
          desc: '''A request to an *address no register maps*, within the address bits the register block decodes, shall get an error response.'''
          source: [
            '''[Explicit Error Cases](hw/ip/tlul/README.md#explicit-error-cases)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["errors as the register checker predicts", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''The CSR checker's error checks require `d_error` 1 on an address no register maps.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_BUS_11
          desc: '''A write answered with an error for any reason other than a failed integrity check shall change no register.'''
          source: [
            '''[cip_base_vseq](hw/dv/sv/cip_lib/README.md#cip_base_vseq)'''
            '''[Error responses](util/reggen/README.md#error-responses)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "bus"
          checks: ["error write changes nothing", "the CSR checker"]
          why: '''An error write is no accepted write, so the CSR checker and the attribute and AON no-write checks hold every register.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "2"
          security: true
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
      ]
    }
    {
      name: '''Wakeup detectors'''
      conditions: [
        '''`w` is a detector (0 to 7); a cycle is a `clk_aon_i` cycle; the watched signal and the forwarded value are defined in the Terms.'''
        '''Register values are those the AON logic holds once a write has crossed. The rows hold with the mode unchanged while enabled, the other fields free to change.'''
        '''They hold whatever `sleep_en_i`, `clk_i` (stopped included) and the scan mode do, except scan mode True while the detector watches a scan clock pad.'''
        '''They are checked from the filter's fourth sample after `rst_aon_ni`. The timed rows (`REQ_WKUP_09a` to `REQ_WKUP_10b`) hold for `CNT_TH` 1 and above.'''
      ]
      requirements: [
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_01
          desc: '''With `MIODIO` 0, the watched signal shall be MIO pad `PADSEL` - 2 for `PADSEL` 2 to 13, and the constant 0 or 1 for `PADSEL` 0 or 1.'''
          source: [
            '''!!MIO_PERIPH_INSEL.IN'''
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MIODIO'''
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR_PADSEL.SEL'''
            '''[Retention and Wakeup Features](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#retention-and-wakeup-features)'''
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_pads`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["edge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_EdgeSetsCause)", "timed high sets cause (assert_Wakeup_TimedHighSetsCause)", "timed low sets cause (assert_Wakeup_TimedLowSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''The checks watch the MIO pad or constant the select names.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_02
          desc: '''With `MIODIO` 1, the watched signal shall be DIO pad `PADSEL` for `PADSEL` 0 to 72.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MIODIO'''
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR_PADSEL.SEL'''
            '''[MIO and DIO Signal Categories](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#mio-and-dio-signal-categories)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_dio_pads`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["edge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_EdgeSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''The checks watch the forwarded value of the DIO pad the select names.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_03
          desc: '''A `PADSEL` that names no pad (14 to 127 with `MIODIO` 0, 73 to 127 with `MIODIO` 1) shall give the watched signal 0.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR_PADSEL.SEL'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `n_mio_pads`, `n_dio_pads`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["timed low sets cause (assert_Wakeup_TimedLowSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''The checks watch 0 on a select that names no pad, so mode 4 must fire and no edge may set the bit.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_04
          desc: '''With `FILTER` 0, the forwarded value shall be the watched signal as sampled at each `clk_aon_i` edge.'''
          source: [
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["edge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_EdgeSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''With `FILTER` 0 the forwarded value the checks watch is the pad as sampled, up to 4 cycles late.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_05
          desc: '''With `FILTER` 1, the forwarded value shall take a new value only once 4 samples in a row have had it.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.FILTER'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["edge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_EdgeSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''A level held for 4 samples is an edge of the forwarded value, and a 3-sample glitch is none.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_06a
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 0 (Posedge) shall detect every rise of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["posedge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_PosedgeSetsCause)"]
          why: '''It wants a hardware write of 1 within 8 cycles of each rise of the forwarded value, a one-sample pulse included, with `EN` 1 then and 4 cycles on.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_06b
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 0 (Posedge) shall detect only at a rise of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''In mode 0 it refuses a hardware write of 1 to a cause bit at 0 that no rise of the forwarded value, seen up to 4 cycles late with `EN` 1, answers.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_07a
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 1 (Negedge) shall detect every fall of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["negedge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_NegedgeSetsCause)"]
          why: '''It wants a hardware write of 1 to bit `w` within 8 cycles of each fall of the forwarded value with `EN` 1 then and for 4 more cycles.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_07b
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 1 (Negedge) shall detect only at a fall of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''In mode 1 it refuses a hardware write of 1 to a cause bit at 0 that no fall of the forwarded value answers: a detector that fires on a rise fails it.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_08a
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 2 (Edge) shall detect every change of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["edge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_EdgeSetsCause)"]
          why: '''It wants a hardware write of 1 to bit `w` within 8 cycles of each rise and each fall of the forwarded value with `EN` 1 then and for 4 more cycles.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_08b
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 2 (Edge) shall detect only at a change of the forwarded value.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''In mode 2 it refuses a hardware write of 1 to a cause bit at 0 that no rise or fall of the forwarded value answers.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_09a
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 3 (TimedHigh) shall detect when the forwarded value has been 1 for `CNT_TH` cycles in a row.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR_CNT_TH.TH'''
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `wkup_cnt_width`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["timed high sets cause (assert_Wakeup_TimedHighSetsCause)"]
          why: '''It wants the cause bit set within 8 cycles of the forwarded value 1 for `CNT_TH` + 1 cycles in a row with `EN` 1, the later count allowed.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_09b
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 3 (TimedHigh) shall *never detect* while the forwarded value has been 1 for fewer than `CNT_TH` cycles in a row.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `wkup_cnt_width`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''In mode 3 it refuses a set of the cause bit while the forwarded value has been 1 for fewer than `CNT_TH` cycles in a row with `EN` 1.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_10a
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 4 (TimedLow) shall detect when the forwarded value has been 0 for `CNT_TH` cycles in a row.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR_CNT_TH.TH'''
            '''[Wakeup Detectors](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/doc/theory_of_operation.md#wakeup-detectors)'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `wkup_cnt_width`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["timed low sets cause (assert_Wakeup_TimedLowSetsCause)"]
          why: '''It wants the cause bit set within 8 cycles of the forwarded value 0 for `CNT_TH` + 1 cycles in a row with `EN` 1, the later count allowed.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_10b
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 4 (TimedLow) shall *never detect* while the forwarded value has been 0 for fewer than `CNT_TH` cycles in a row.'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
            '''[top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson `wkup_cnt_width`](hw/top_darjeeling/ip_autogen/pinmux/data/top_darjeeling_pinmux.ipconfig.hjson)'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''In mode 4 it refuses a set of the cause bit while the forwarded value has been 0 for fewer than `CNT_TH` cycles in a row with `EN` 1.'''
          milestone: "V2"
          priority: "1"
          security: false
          state: "open: not reviewed for this top"
        }
        {
          name: REQ_WKUP_11
          desc: '''An enabled detector in mode 5, 6 or 7 shall detect exactly the rises of the forwarded value, as in mode 0 (Posedge).'''
          source: [
            '''!!WKUP_DETECTOR.MODE'''
          ]
          kind: "spec"
          testpoint: "wakeup"
          checks: ["posedge sets cause (assert_Wakeup_PosedgeSetsCause)", "no false cause (assert_Wakeup_NoFalseCause)"]
          why: '''Both checks read `MODE` 5, 6 and 7 as mode 0.'''
